cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Alert-Budget-Aware Evaluation for Transaction Monitoring:
  an evaluation harness for AML models on IBM AMLworld
message: >-
  If you use this software or its findings, please cite it, and cite the
  AMLworld dataset separately — it is a distinct artifact under a different
  licence and is not redistributed here.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Thirupallikrishnan
    given-names: Nirmal Kumar
repository-code: "https://github.com/NirmalKumar31/aml-evaluation-harness-public"
license: MIT
version: 0.1.2
date-released: "2026-09-17"
keywords:
  - anti-money-laundering
  - evaluation methodology
  - alert budget
  - class imbalance
  - baseline strength
abstract: >-
  A measurement harness for anti-money-laundering transaction monitoring on the
  IBM AMLworld synthetic benchmark. It reports detection under a fixed daily
  review budget on an (account, calendar-day) alert unit, against explicit
  nulls and ceilings, using a ring-participant-disjoint temporal split. Its
  headline result is about the benchmark rather than about a model: on
  HI-Medium a 32-feature logistic regression reaches precision@50 = 0.5706 at
  an operationally motivated alert-budget operating point, against an
  eight-seed gradient-boosted mean of 0.8248 with observed range 0.5914-0.8981.
  A strong linear baseline on this representation bounds what a headline score
  from this benchmark demonstrates about a method.
